\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\lang9 Complete 12-Week Brian Alsruhe-Inspired Conditioning & Strength Program\par
This complete, printable 12-week program combines high work-capacity Giant Sets (four exercises performed sequentially with minimal rest) with a structured periodization scheme. Rest 90\f1\endash 120 seconds only after completing all movements in a Giant Set.\par
1. Program Overview & Mechanics\par
How Giant Sets WorkEach primary lifting session centers around a Giant Set containing four distinct elements performed back-to-back:Antagonist / Explosive: A movement opposing the main lift or an explosive power jump/throw.Main Strength Lift: Executed using the designated percentage of your Training Max (TM).Core / Trunk: Heavy, anti-rotational, or rotational core work.Active Rest / Conditioning: Low-impact cardio movement to keep the heart rate elevated.Understanding Percentages & Training Max (TM)Percentages dictate the weight used for main lifts based on your Training Max (TM), which prevents overtraining and allows safe re-adaptation to heavy loading.Calculating TM: Take 85% to 90% of your current, realistic 1-Rep Max (1RM).$$\\text\{Training Max (TM)\} = \\text\{Current 1RM\} \\times 0.85$$Example: If your current Bench Press 1RM is 200 lbs, your TM is $200 \\times 0.85 = 170\\text\{ lbs\}$.On Dynamic / Speed Days (Days 4 & 5), use a flat 60%\endash 70% of TM across all 12 weeks with an emphasis on speed and acceleration.For Assistance Work, select weights that leave 2\endash 3 clean reps in reserve (RPE 7\endash 8).2. Weekly Master ScheduleDayFocusPrimary ObjectiveDay 1: MondayMax Effort Lower (Squat Focus)Heavy Lower Giant Set + Core + ConditioningDay 2: TuesdayMax Effort Upper (Overhead Press Focus)Heavy Upper Giant Set + Upper Density TripletDay 3: WednesdayActive Recovery 1Low-Impact Zone 2 Aerobic Base & MobilityDay 4: ThursdayDynamic / Speed Lower (Deadlift Focus)Dynamic Speed Pulls + Unilateral WorkDay 5: FridayDynamic / Speed Upper (Bench Focus)Dynamic Pressing + Pulling DensityDay 6: SaturdayActive Recovery 2Loaded Carries, Strongman GPP & Work CapacityDay 7: SundayFull RestTotal Physical & Neurological Recovery3. 12-Week Main Lift Progression MatrixApply these percentage and set/rep targets to your main lifts: Barbell Back Squat (Day 1), Overhead Press (Day 2), Deadlift (Day 4), and Bench Press (Day 5).WeekBlock / PhaseSets & RepsIntensity (% of TM)Rest IntervalPhase ObjectiveW1Wave 1: Hypertrophy4 sets x 8 reps65%90 secWork capacity & volumeW2Wave 1: Hypertrophy4 sets x 8 reps70%90 secWork capacity & volumeW3Wave 1: Hypertrophy4 sets x 6 reps75%90 secPeak volume loadW4Deload3 sets x 6 reps50%120 secDeload / Technique focusW5Wave 2: Strength4 sets x 5 reps75%120 secStrength base buildingW6Wave 2: Strength4 sets x 5 reps80%120 secStrength intensificationW7Wave 2: Strength4 sets x 3 reps85%120 secHeavy strength densityW8Deload3 sets x 5 reps55%120 secDeload / Joint recoveryW9Wave 3: Realization3x3 @ 80%, 1x3+ (AMRAP)85%150 secHigh intensity effortW10Wave 3: Realization3x2 @ 85%, 1x2+ (AMRAP)90%150 secHigh intensity effortW11Wave 3: Realization2x1 @ 90%, 1x1+ (AMRAP)95%180 secPeak strength outputW12Test / ResetWork to safe 1RM or 3x360%FlexibleRe-test baselines or deloadNote: AMRAP = "As Many Reps As Possible" with strict, technically sound form.4. Daily Workout TemplatesDay 1: Max Effort Lower (Squat Focus)1. Warm-Up (2 Rounds, Minimal Rest):Goblet Squats x 10 reps (3-second pause at bottom)Hanging Leg Raises x 10 repsKettlebell / Steel Mace Swings x 15 reps2. Main Strength Giant Set (4 Sets Total):A. Explosive: Broad Jump x 3 reps (or Box Jump x 3)B. Main Lift: Barbell Back Squat (Refer to Progression Matrix for sets/reps/%)C. Core: Ab Wheel Rollout or Hanging Toes-to-Bar x 8\endash 10 repsD. Active Rest: Jump Rope or Light Kettlebell Swings x 45 secondsRest 90\endash 120 seconds after movement D, then repeat.3. Assistance Block (3 Rounds):Barbell Romanian Deadlift (RDL) or Zercher Good Mornings x 8\endash 10 repsBulgarian Split Squats or Walking Lunges x 10 reps per legHeavy Plank Hold x 45 secondsRest 90 seconds between rounds.4. Conditioning Finisher (10-Minute EMOM):Every Minute on the Minute for 10 Minutes:5 Kettlebell / Dumbbell Clean & Presses8\endash 10 BurpeesRest for the remainder of each minute.Day 2: Max Effort Upper (Overhead Press Focus)1. Warm-Up (2 Rounds, Minimal Rest):Band Pull-Aparts x 20 repsScapular Pull-ups x 10 repsBear Crawl x 50 feet2. Main Strength Giant Set (4 Sets Total):A. Antagonist: Weighted Pull-Up or Heavy Lat Pulldown x 5\endash 8 repsB. Main Lift: Overhead Barbell Press (Refer to Progression Matrix for sets/reps/%)C. Core: Dragon Flags or Heavy Hanging Knee Raises x 8\endash 10 repsD. Active Rest: Battle Ropes or Shadow Boxing x 45 secondsRest 90\endash 120 seconds after movement D, then repeat.3. Assistance Giant Set (3 Rounds):Incline Dumbbell Bench Press x 10\endash 12 repsBent-Over Barbell Row or T-Bar Row x 10\endash 12 repsHalf-Kneeling Bottoms-Up Kettlebell Press x 8 reps per sideFace Pulls x 15\endash 20 repsRest 90 seconds between rounds.4. Conditioning Finisher (8-Minute AMRAP):As Many Rounds As Possible in 8 Minutes:10 Dumbbell Thrusters10 Push-ups10 Ring Rows or Inverted RowsDay 3: Active Recovery & Aerobic Base1. Steady-State Zone 2 Aerobic Base (30\endash 45 Minutes):Maintain steady effort via Rucking, Rowing, Stationary Bike, or Incline Walking. Keep heart rate low enough to maintain a conversation without gasping.2. Mobility & Thoracic Flow (15 Minutes):World's Greatest Stretch x 5 per sideCouch Stretch x 60 seconds per sideDeep Squat Pry x 2 minutes3. Core & Grip Work (3 Sets):Dead Hang from Pull-Up Bar x Max TimeSuitcase Hold x 45 seconds per sideDay 4: Dynamic / Speed Lower (Deadlift Focus)1. Warm-Up (2 Rounds, Minimal Rest):Single-Leg Glute Bridge x 10 reps per sideResistance Band Good Mornings x 15 repsBirddogs x 8 reps per side2. Speed Giant Set (5 Sets Total):A. Explosive: Kettlebell Snatch or Kettlebell Swings x 5 repsB. Main Lift: Deadlift x 3 reps @ 60%\endash 70% TM (Focus on maximal bar speed)C. Core: Landmine Twists or Heavy Pallof Press x 8 reps per sideD. Active Rest: Jumping Jacks or A-Skips x 45 secondsRest 90 seconds after movement D, then repeat.3. Volume Triplet (3 Rounds):Safety Squat Bar or Goblet Front Squats x 10\endash 12 repsHamstring Curls (Band or Machine) x 15 repsHeavy Farmers Carry x 100 feetRest 90 seconds between rounds.4. Conditioning Finisher ("Death by Kettlebell Swings"):Min 1: 10 Swings | Min 2: 12 Swings | Min 3: 14 Swings...Add 2 reps every minute until you can no longer complete the required reps within that minute.Day 5: Dynamic / Speed Upper (Bench Focus)1. Warm-Up (2 Rounds, Minimal Rest):Push-up to Downward Dog x 8 repsCuban Rotations (Light) x 12 repsBand Dislocates x 15 reps2. Speed Giant Set (5 Sets Total):A. Antagonist: Chest-Supported Dumbbell Row x 8 repsB. Main Lift: Barbell Bench Press x 3\endash 5 reps @ 60%\endash 70% TM (Focus on maximal bar speed)C. Core: Ab Mat Sit-ups with Overhead Plate x 12 repsD. Active Rest: Row, SkiErg, or Medicine Ball Slams x 10 repsRest 90 seconds after movement D, then repeat.3. Volume Triplet (3 Rounds):Standing Dumbbell Overhead Press x 10\endash 12 repsChin-ups x Max Reps (or Band-Assisted to 10 reps)Dips x 10\endash 12 repsRest 90 seconds between rounds.4. Conditioning Finisher (10-Minute Chipper for Time):50 Alternating Dumbbell Snatches40 Hand-Release Push-ups30 Dumbbell Goblet Squats20 Burpees Over DumbbellDay 6: Active Recovery & Strongman / GPP1. Loaded Carry Circuit (4 Rounds):Perform continuously; rest 2 minutes after completing each full round:Heavy Farmers Walk x 100 feetSandbag / Keg / Heavy Med-Ball Bear-Hug Carry x 100 feetOverhead Waiter's Walk x 50 feet (Right) / 50 feet (Left)Sled Push or Heavy Tire Flip x 100 feet2. Trunk & GPP Finisher (3 Sets):Side Plank x 45 seconds per sideSledgehammer Tire Strikes or Steel Mace Swings x 20 reps per sideLight Sled Drag / Walking x 5 minutes continuousDay 7: Sunday Full RestTotal Recovery Day: Zero structured lifting or high-intensity cardio. Focus on adequate hydration, protein intake, and optimal sleep.\f0\par
